\subsection{Phase C: exact large-angle $\SO(3)$ measurement dissipation}
\label{sec:stability-widening-phase-c}

The deployed nonlinear certificate is stated directly on the rotation group and
on the source-reachable Kalman correction.  No common-radius or componentwise
radius relaxation is used in the primary certificate chain.  Velocity,
position, integral displacement, latent acceleration, and accelerometer bias
remain in the exact source state and covariance recursion; their influence on
attitude is retained through the actual accepted innovations and Kalman gains.

Let
\begin{equation}
 \mat R_e:=\widehat{\mat R}\mat R^\top\in\SO(3),
 \qquad
 V_R(\mat R_e):=\frac12\operatorname{tr}(\mat I-\mat R_e)
 =1-\cos\theta_e,
 \label{eq:widen-SO3-energy}
\end{equation}
where $\theta_e\in[0,\pi]$ is the geodesic attitude error.  Define also
\begin{equation}
 \vct e_R:=\operatorname{vex}\!\left(
 \frac{\mat R_e-\mat R_e^\top}{2}\right)
 =\sin\theta_e\,\vct u_e.
 \label{eq:widen-SO3-gradient}
\end{equation}
For every fixed $0<\theta_*<\pi$ and
$0\le\theta_e\le\theta_*$,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1-\cos\theta_*}{\theta_*^2}\theta_e^2
 \le V_R(\mat R_e)\le\frac12\theta_e^2.
 \label{eq:widen-SO3-sector}
\end{equation}
Thus $V_R$ is a nonlocal attitude energy on every compact geodesic chart that
stays strictly away from the antipodal set.

At an accepted correction, use the exact source residuals and gains and write
\begin{equation}
 \vct d_k:=\Delta\vct\theta_k
 =\mat E_\theta\left(
 \mat K_{a,k}\vct r_{a,k}
 +\mat K_{m,k}\vct r_{m,k}
 +\mat K_{S,k}\vct r_{S,k}\right),
 \qquad \vct r_{S,k}=-\delta\vct S.
 \label{eq:widen-exact-source-correction}
\end{equation}
Rejected updates contribute the corresponding zero term.  Equation
\eqref{eq:widen-exact-source-correction} retains the full $S\to\theta$
cross-covariance path and all non-attitude contributions to the accepted
accelerometer residual; no block-diagonal or Schmidt-style correction is
introduced for the proof.

The source calls \texttt{quat\_from\_delta\_theta}.  Outside its small series
branch the injected rotation is exactly
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal R(q_c(\vct d))=\exp([\vct d]_\times),}
 \label{eq:widen-exact-injection}
\end{equation}
and the normalized series branch differs from that exponential by a sixth-order
geodesic defect:
\begin{equation}
 d_{\SO(3)}\!\left(
 \mathcal R(q_c(\vct d)),\exp([\vct d]_\times)\right)
 \le c_s\|\vct d\|^6,
 \qquad \|\vct d\|\le10^{-2}.
 \label{eq:widen-series-defect}
\end{equation}
The series defect is carried as a bounded source perturbation in the word-level
certificate below rather than replacing the finite correction by a local
first-order reset.

Ignoring only the explicit series defect for the moment, the physical attitude
error after the left correction is
\begin{equation}
 \mat R_e^+=\exp([\vct d_k]_\times)\mat R_e^-.
 \label{eq:widen-exact-attitude-update}
\end{equation}
Let $\delta_k:=\|\vct d_k\|$ and define the continuous functions
$\operatorname{sinc}\delta:=\sin\delta/\delta$ and
$\operatorname{cosc}\delta:=(1-\cos\delta)/\delta^2$ with their limiting values
at zero.  Rodrigues' identity gives the exact finite-correction energy change
\begin{align}
 V_R(\mat R_e^+)-V_R(\mat R_e^-)
 &=\operatorname{sinc}(\delta_k)\,
   \vct d_k^\top\vct e_R^-
 \nonumber\\
 &\quad-\frac12\operatorname{cosc}(\delta_k)
   \operatorname{tr}\!\left(
   [\vct d_k]_\times^2\mat R_e^-\right).
 \label{eq:widen-exact-energy-change}
\end{align}
Equation~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change} is exact for arbitrary finite
$\vct d_k$ and does not replace $\sin\theta_e$ by $\theta_e$ or bound the
finite correction by a generic quadratic Taylor remainder.

\begin{lemma}[Exact finite-correction group identity]
\label{lem:widen-exact-group-identity}
For every $\mat R_e\in\SO(3)$ and every finite correction $\vct d$, the update
of Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-attitude-update} satisfies
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change}.  Hence the sign of the actual
attitude-energy change can be certified directly from the implemented
innovation and gain rather than inferred from a norm bound on
$\|\vct d\|^2$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Substitute Rodrigues' formula
$\exp([d]_\times)=I+\operatorname{sinc}(\delta)[d]_\times+
\operatorname{cosc}(\delta)[d]_\times^2$ into
$V_R(R^+)-V_R(R^-)=-\tfrac12\operatorname{tr}((\exp([d]_\times)-I)R^-)$.  The
identity
$\operatorname{tr}([d]_\times R)=-2d^\top
\operatorname{vex}((R-R^\top)/2)$ gives the first term and the second Rodrigues
term gives the remaining trace exactly.
\end{proof}

The implemented covariance reset is
\begin{equation}
 \mat G_r(\vct d)=\mat I+\frac12[\vct d]_\times,
 \label{eq:widen-reset-G}
\end{equation}
with
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\mat G_r(\vct d)\|_2
 =\sqrt{1+\frac14\|\vct d\|^2},
 \qquad
 \det\mat G_r=1+\frac14\|\vct d\|^2>0.}
 \label{eq:widen-reset-G-bound}
\end{equation}
Thus neither the state injection nor the covariance reset has a singularity at
an unwrapped correction norm of $\pi$.

\subsubsection{Source-faithful large-angle dissipation sector}

Let $\vct\xi$ collect the non-attitude active error coordinates in the current
fixed-dimensional Live mode.  For every admitted source tuple $g$ (covariance,
accepted-update pattern, measured vector geometry, OU/$R_S$ parameters,
pseudo-update phase, and gain), define the exact correction map
\begin{equation}
 \vct d_g(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 :=\mat E_\theta\left(
 \mat K_a\vct r_a(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 +\mat K_m\vct r_m(\mat R_e)
 -\mat K_S\delta\vct S\right).
 \label{eq:widen-source-correction-map}
\end{equation}
All quantities in one evaluation of Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-source-correction-map}
come from the same source-reachable tuple; independent gain extrema are never
combined.

For a compact source node $i$ and an angle $0<\theta_{*,i}<\pi$, let
$\mathcal A_i$ be the corresponding exact source family satisfying
$\theta_e\le\theta_{*,i}$, the declared measurement gates, covariance bounds,
and finite correction bound.  Define
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr D_{R,g}(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 :=V_R(\mat R_e)-
 V_R\!\left(
 \exp([\vct d_g(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)]_\times)\mat R_e\right).
 \label{eq:widen-group-dissipation}
\end{equation}
A source node satisfies the \emph{large-angle correction sector} when there are
$\alpha_{R,i}>0$ and $\beta_{R,i}<\infty$ such that, for every admissible tuple
and every state in $\mathcal A_i$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathscr D_{R,g}(\mat R_e,\vct\xi)
 \ge \alpha_{R,i}V_R(\mat R_e)
      -\beta_{R,i}\|\vct\xi\|^2.}
 \label{eq:widen-large-angle-sector}
\end{equation}
The inequality is evaluated with the exact finite-correction expression
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-exact-energy-change}.  It therefore credits dissipative
innovation directions and penalizes gain-coupled non-attitude errors only by
the amount they actually perturb the group energy.

\begin{theorem}[Large-angle source correction dissipation]
\label{thm:widen-large-angle-dissipation}
Suppose a fixed-dimensional normal-Live source node satisfies
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-sector} on
$\theta_e\le\theta_{*,i}<\pi$.  Include the series-branch defect of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-series-defect} and bounded deterministic model error in the
source disturbance budget.  Then every accepted correction in that node obeys
\begin{equation}
 V_R^+\le(1-\alpha_{R,i})V_R^-
 +\beta_{R,i}\|\vct\xi^-\|^2+\gamma_{R,i}(\bar d),
 \label{eq:widen-large-angle-bound}
\end{equation}
for a finite class-$\mathcal K$ function $\gamma_{R,i}$ on the declared compact
source family.  The admissible attitude domain is set by the verified geodesic
chart and source dissipation sector, not by a small-angle Taylor radius.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Equation~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-sector} and the definition
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-group-dissipation} give the zero-disturbance decrease
exactly.  The complete correction map and $V_R$ are smooth on the compact
source family with $\theta_e<\pi$ and finite correction norm, hence the bounded
series/model perturbation changes the endpoint energy by a uniformly bounded
class-$\mathcal K$ amount.  Rearrangement yields
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-bound}.
\end{proof}

The condition is deliberately source faithful.  It does not assume that the
attitude rows of the Kalman gain form a scalar Wahba gradient, and it does not
discard the $S\to\theta$ path.  For a particular deployed source family the
largest certifiable $\theta_{*,i}$ is the largest geodesic angle for which the
rigorous lower bound in Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-sector} remains
positive.  The value may approach $\pi$ from below, but the antipodal topology
and any genuine measurement critical set remain excluded; no global MEKF claim
is made.
